# Excalidraw Architecture

## State Management

- Custom state via actionManager — NOT Redux/Zustand/MobX
- Prefer actionManager.dispatch() for scene/editor mutations tied to `AppState` (`packages/excalidraw/types.ts`); local component state via `this.setState()` is acceptable for instance-scoped UI state (for example `contextMenu`, `activeEmbeddable`, `editingFrame`, `bindMode`, `selectedLinearElement`, `errorMessage`)
- State type: AppState (packages/excalidraw/types.ts)

## Rendering

- Canvas 2D rendering — NOT React DOM for drawing
- Render pipeline: Scene → renderScene() → canvas context
- DO NOT use react-konva, fabric.js, pixi.js

## Dependencies

- No new npm packages without explicit approval
- Check packages/utils/ before adding external helpers

## How to verify

- Dependency changes: inspect `package.json` / `yarn.lock` in the PR — new packages need explicit approval; prefer `packages/utils/` (or existing internals) before adding externals.
- State and mutations: code review that scene/editor mutations go through `actionManager` / documented sync paths, while local instance-scoped UI state remains on `this.setState()` instead of new ad-hoc stores (see `AGENTS.md` for ActionManager and `syncActionResult()`).
- Build sanity: `yarn test:typecheck` and `yarn build` (or `yarn build:packages` when only packages change) from the repo root.
